---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Plate from '../components/Plate.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const principles = [
  {
    title: 'Curation',
    body: [
      'We take on few objects. An object is accepted because it is worth owning, not because it will move.',
      'That means declining a good deal of perfectly saleable material, and it means the catalogue is often short.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Authenticity',
    body: [
      'Attribution, condition and restoration are described as they are, at the point of sale, in writing.',
      'Where something is uncertain, the entry says it is uncertain. Where an opinion is one specialist’s rather than a settled view, the entry says whose.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'History',
    body: [
      'Ownership history is researched before an object is offered, and the records are supplied with it.',
      'The documentary position is the part of an object that cannot be improved later. It is where most of our time goes.',
    ],
  },
];

const roles = [
  {
    title: 'Curator',
    body: 'Selecting, researching and cataloguing objects to a consistent standard, whether they are worth one thousand pounds or one hundred thousand.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Dealer',
    body: 'Holding objects on our own account and offering them openly, with our interest disclosed.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Sourcing house',
    body: 'Acting for collectors who are looking for something specific, through channels that are not public.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Collector service',
    body: 'Advising on collections already assembled: documentation, condition, insurance valuation, division and eventual sale.',
  },
];
---

<Page
  title="About"
  heading="Featherstone Vaults."
  eyebrow="The house"
  description="Featherstone Vaults is a curator, dealer and private sourcing house for significant historical and scientific objects. The Cotswolds, working internationally."
  path="/about"
  standfirst="A private dealer and collection house for historically, scientifically and culturally significant objects. We work from the Cotswolds with collectors internationally."
  trail={[{ label: 'About', href: '/about' }]}
  headingWidth="16ch"
>
  <div class="shell">
    <!-- Principles ------------------------------------------------ -->
    <section class="rule-t pt-12" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
      <h2 id="principles-heading" class="label-sm text-bronze-lit">Three principles</h2>
      <dl class="mt-12 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-12 md:grid-cols-3">
        {
          principles.map((p, i) => (
            <div class="rule-t pt-6">
              <p class="label-sm tnum text-ash">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</p>
              <dt class="display-2 mt-4 text-ivory">{p.title}</dt>
              <dd class="prose-fv mt-5 max-w-none">
                {p.body.map((line) => (
                  <p>{line}</p>
                ))}
              </dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <!-- What we are ----------------------------------------------- -->
    <section class="pt-24 md:pt-32" aria-labelledby="roles-heading">
      <div class="grid gap-x-16 gap-y-10 rule-t pt-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <h2 id="roles-heading" class="label-sm text-bronze-lit lg:col-span-3">What we are</h2>
        <div class="lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-4">
          <p class="prose-fv max-w-[40rem]">
            Featherstone Vaults operates in four capacities. They overlap, and we are explicit
            about which one applies to any given object or conversation.
          </p>
          <dl class="mt-10 max-w-[40rem]">
            {
              roles.map((r) => (
                <div class="rule-soft-t py-6">
                  <dt class="display-3 text-ivory">{r.title}</dt>
                  <dd class="prose-fv mt-3">{r.body}</dd>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Training --------------------------------------------------- -->
    <section class="pt-24 md:pt-32" aria-labelledby="training-heading">
      <div class="grid gap-x-16 gap-y-10 rule-t pt-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <h2 id="training-heading" class="label-sm text-bronze-lit lg:col-span-3">Training</h2>
        <div class="lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-4">
          <p class="prose-fv max-w-[40rem]">
            Featherstone Vaults is run by Thomas Featherstone, who holds a Diploma in
            Palaeontology and a Diploma in Geology.
          </p>
          <dl class="mt-10 max-w-[40rem]">
            <div class="rule-soft-t py-6">
              <dt class="display-3 text-ivory">Diploma in Palaeontology</dt>
              <dd class="prose-fv mt-3">
                The fossil record and how it is read: what a specimen is, how it was formed and
                what can reasonably be claimed about it.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-soft-t py-6">
              <dt class="display-3 text-ivory">Diploma in Geology</dt>
              <dd class="prose-fv mt-3">
                Origins, plate tectonics, rocks and minerals, volcanism, seismicity, weathering and
                geological analysis.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <div class="prose-fv mt-10 max-w-[40rem]">
            <p>
              That training bears directly on the natural history department: how a specimen is
              identified, where it formed, how it was prepared, and what has been done to it since
              it came out of the ground.
            </p>
            <p>
              It does not extend to every department, and we do not pretend otherwise. Where an
              object sits outside it, the assessment is made with specialist help and the entry
              records whose opinion it rests on.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a href="/provenance-authenticity" class="action-quiet mt-9">How we assess an object</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Cotswolds ---------------------------------------------- -->
    <section class="pt-24 md:pt-32" aria-labelledby="place-heading">
      <div class="grid items-center gap-x-16 gap-y-12 rule-t pt-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="lg:col-span-6">
          <h2 id="place-heading" class="display-1 max-w-[14ch] text-ivory">
            Rooted in history. At home in the Cotswolds.
          </h2>
          <p class="prose-fv mt-8">A local presence. A global perspective.</p>
          <p class="prose-fv mt-5">
            Objects are held, examined and photographed here. Collectors are welcome by
            appointment, and a great many transactions are concluded without anyone travelling at
            all. Where an object should be seen in person before a decision, we will say so.
          </p>
          <p class="label-sm mt-10 text-ash">
            {SITE.locality}<span class="mx-3 opacity-50" aria-hidden="true">·</span>{SITE.country}
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-6">
          <Plate ratio="4 / 3" tone="3" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 46vw, 100vw" />
          <p class="meta mt-4 text-ash">Photography of the premises to follow.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Working with us -------------------------------------------- -->
    <section class="pt-24 pb-24 md:pt-32 md:pb-32" aria-labelledby="working-heading">
      <div class="rule-t pt-12">
        <div class="grid gap-x-16 gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
          <h2 id="working-heading" class="label-sm text-bronze-lit lg:col-span-3">
            Working with us
          </h2>
          <div class="lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-4">
            <div class="prose-fv max-w-[40rem]">
              <p>
                There is no membership, no minimum and no pressure to move quickly. Collectors at
                the beginning of a collection are as welcome as institutions, and the standard of
                cataloguing is the same either way.
              </p>
              <p>
                The one thing we ask is directness. Tell us what you are actually looking for and
                what you are prepared to spend, and we will tell you honestly whether we can help.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-start gap-5 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap sm:items-center sm:gap-8">
              <a href="/enquire" class="action action-solid">Make an enquiry</a>
              <a href="/provenance-authenticity" class="action-quiet">Our standards</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Page>
